 ],
 "notes": "Scope: text 3 only (research/studies/laestrygonians/article.md), covering the abstract (RU + EN, keywords), §§ 1–6, notes 1–38 and appendix blocks appx-1…appx-12. The bibliography and modern scholars/editors (Dindorf, Carnuth, Lehrs, Mette, Broggiato, Bilić, Buttmann, Porson, Aldus, etc.) are excluded. No file was modified.\n\nAuthors: 27, kind \"author\". Socrates and Odysseus/Ulixes appear only as characters, so they are not indexed. The scholiasts and the B interpolator are anonymous; their collections are works with author_id \"anon\". \"anon\" is a placeholder, not an entry in the authors list.\n\nPatterns: tested with a scanner that matches at word start, one hit per unit. Text-units hit per author:\n- homer 9, crates 19, aristarchus 11, geminus 11, eustathius 10, aratus 10, strabo 8, aristonicus 6, gellius 5, hipparchus 4, polybius 3\n- pytheas 2, eudoxus 2, attalus-rhodes 2, herodicus 2, eratosthenes 2, apollodorus 2, athenaeus 2\n- 1 each: hesiod, plato, thucydides, cicero, horace, claudius-ptolemy, cleanthes, aristyllus, boethus\n\nPattern decisions:\n- Patterns are case-sensitive, so adjectives are not counted (\"кратетовское\", \"гомеровские\", \"аратовское\", \"гиппарховы\"). The one exception is Plato, who appears only as \"платоновского «Пира»\".\n- \"Кратет(?!ов)\" excludes the capitalised \"Кратетовское\" (§ 1) and \"Кратетовец\" (n14, Herodicus).\n- Greek \"Κράτων\" is included. It is the Moscow codex's spelling of Crates' name (n19).\n- The bare-word stem \"Hipparch\" does not match the satellite catalogue \"Hipparcos\" (n18).\n\nCross-text collisions: I also checked all patterns against zacher-1.json and odyssey-10.njk.\n- Zacher's Attalus (the Macedonian noble) and Ptolemy (Soter) would collide with entries here. The ids are therefore \"attalus-rhodes\" (restricted to the forms Атталом/Атталу/\"Аттал… Родосск\") and \"claudius-ptolemy\" (with exclude regexes for the Zacher ch. 17 passage). Both now give 0 Zacher hits.\n- The Homer, Aristarchus, Eratosthenes, Strabo and Thucydides hits on the odyssey-10 page are the same persons.\n\nWikidata: every Q-id was confirmed with wbsearchentities plus wbgetentities, or a haswbstatement:P50 author search.\n- Hipparchus' commentary Q42196579 and Geminus' Isagoge Q111686266 (\"Introduction to astronomy\") were found through P50.\n- Herodicus' Πρὸς τὸν Φιλοσωκράτην has a duplicate item, Q141712887; I used the older Q130297888.\n- No item was found for the scholia on the Odyssey, the scholia on Aratus, Aristonicus' Περὶ σημείων, or the fragment collections. The Q138720617 \"Scholia D in Odysseam\" item was deliberately not used for the whole corpus.\n- No places were indexed, so pleiades is \"\" throughout.\n\nLocus normalisation:\n- Book letters are converted to numbers (κ 190 → 10.190; δ 556 → 4.556; Alm. II.6 → 2.6).\n- Eustathius is cited by Rome-edition page (1648, 1649, 1648.42).\n- Fragment numbers are given bare under the separate works crates-fr-broggiato, crates-fr-mette and herodic-fr.\n\nJudgement calls (worth reviewing):\n1. Od. 10.84 is cited in § 3 for the quoted \"неспящий\" line, although no number is given there.\n2. Quotations inside the appendix scholia are cited as Homer/Aratus loci: Od. 9.473 (appx-4), Od. 10.86 (appx-9), Od. 10.82–85 (appx-12), Arat. 61–62 (appx-9, appx-10). The apparatus at appx-9, \"Ἄρατος] 61 … memorat scholiasta\", is also recorded as schol. Arat. 61.\n3. Footnotes that cite edition lines of an already-identified scholion count as loci: schol. Arat. 62 in n19, n20, n25; Σ Od. 10.86 HQ in n2 and n38. The bare \"схолия\" in n9 is not counted.\n4. \"В главе 16\" in § 3 is given as Gem. locus \"16\".\n5. The Aristonicus record for § 2 has an empty locus (his notes on the Odyssey are cited as a whole: none for κ 70–91).\n6. Cicero's Homeric tag \"Τηλέπυλον Λαιστρυγονίην\" (n35) is not counted as an Odyssey locus.\n7. The Greek title of Düring's «О пирах» is left blank because the article does not give it."
}